st  house atreides a scene that we never see  in vilnews in fact we don't see the  guild navigator at all and the spacing  guild is only mentioned once the emperor  fears house atreides is becoming too  strong duke lado has become increasingly  popular among the houses of the landsrod  and he believes them to be developing a  new weapon that incorporates sound  something that isn't brought up in this  new version fearing his power could be  in jeopardy the emperor joins forces  with vladimir harkenin to lure the  atreides into a trap with arrakis as the  bait in both versions paula tradies has  dreams however in vil news there's a lot  more of them and they're even more  cryptic i'm planning on coming out with  a dune 2021 ending explained soon which  will go over this in more detail the  atreides home planet of kaladin is  explored more openly in 2021 with  sweeping exterior vistas villeneuve also  spends more time developing the  relationships between paul and his  parents something that is brushed aside  rather quickly in 84. and this time  spent on character development really  helps round out the characters who come  across as rather flat in the older  version not mentioned in 84 is paul's  grandfather we see a painting of him  along with matador paraphenalia as seen  not in 1984 is duke lato atreides  accepting control of arrakis by the  herald of the change this also  establishes the atreides family signet  ring which gets passed down to paul and  later to paul's son lado the second we  also get our first look at reverend  mother helen moyim of the bened jesuit  basically these johnny sins looking  women however we never see them without  their head pieces off to determine if  they're bald like in 1984. perhaps one  of the biggest differences is the  absolute glow-up of duncan idaho whose  part is drastically expanded in vilnius  the 1984 version he's in about two  scenes and has little to no interaction  with paul villeneuve takes the time to  craft a friendship between paul and  duncan even foreshadowing duncan's death  when paul says he foresaw it in one of  his dreams villeneuve decides to have  this paul and lado bonding scene outside  the graves of their ancestors whereas in  lynch's version it's overlooking the  ocean both versions have paul training  however you can see the difference 37  years of improvement in visual effects  have had regardless the effect is still  the same with these shields they have  the ability to soften incoming blows  unfortunately we don't get a scene where  paul fights a robot or patrick stewart's  gurney runs into battle holding a pug  yeah that actually happens welcome to  the homeworld of house harkonnen gady  prime and i absolutely love what they  did with baron vladimir harkin in here  in the 84 version he's just so over the  top both in look and mannerisms whereas  skarsgard here plays him more subdued  and restrained the color scheme is also  markedly different with 84s being green  and sickly and villeneuve's dark and  grim we're then introduced to dave  bautista's beast robin vladimir's nephew  i guess i should mention all the  harkening and villeneuve's version are  pale and bald while in lynches he goes  for soulless gingers  i have a soul surprisingly missing from  2021 is fade ralph harkin vladimir's  other nephew who was played by sting in  1984. no word yet if he was cut entirely  or will make an appearance in part two  we also get a look at piter looking very  different than his 1984 counterpart  notice the lack of staining around his  lips which was due to consumption of  sappho juice used to amplify a mentats  mental powers this seems to be replaced  by this black mark under his lips which  the atreides mentat luffy or hawat has  as well you may also notice their eyes  roll to the back of their heads when  accessing information that's because  these mentats are like human  supercomputers computers and ai haven't  really been trusted in the dune universe  since humanity was previously enslaved  by ai and it wasn't until the great  revolt that they were freed something  not mentioned in 2021 before heading to  arrakis lady jessica and lado make love  this is where alia is conceived paul's  future sister we get a brief glimpse of  her in one of paul's dreams in 2021 but  this love scene is omitted we'll see a  kid version of alia in 1984. vilnews  version also places more emphasis on the  fremen locals we see how they're quite  religious and chant listen al gabe  basically the freman word for off-world  prophet paul spends much of his time  studying arrakis but the 84 version has  no mention of the sand walk away the  framing walk to avoid alerting sand  worms in both versions we see an  assassination attempt against paul using  a hunter seeker we never find out who  was responsible for this in the 1984  version but in 2021 we learned a  harkonnen had been living in the walls  for six weeks biding his time this pet  never seen nor this scene between the  baron piper and the reverend mother she  wants to ensure that in the impending  attack that paul and jessica aren't  killed lady jessica is benedescerate  after all thus the reverend mother  believes she has some authority over  what happens to her but the baron finds  a loophole around this he won't kill  paul and jessica he'll just drop them  off in the middle of the desert and let  the blistering sands take them another  big difference is kynes who in the 84  version was played by max fonseido she  is the overseer of change helping  facilitate the transfer of power between  harkonnen and atreides and acting as  sort of a diplomat between the atreides  and the emperor we also get our first  introduction of stilgar one of the  fremen tribe leaders in the 84 version  he never visits duke lado nor do we get  that awesome spinning scene the 2021  version also places more emphasis on  frem and tech like the paracompass  duncan gives paul or the moisture tent  jessica and paul used to survive in the  desert the villeneuve version makes use  of these ornithopters and this is what  they use to get around in lynch's  version this whole spice harvester  rescue scene is different as well  vilnu's version is much more tense  having both paul and lato get out of  their copter to help save these stranded  men in lynches you basically just have  lato yelling at the men to move and when  paul ingests some of the spikes he  experiences more visions and hears the  words quitsat's hararak an old shaksoba  term to describe the chosen one although  he does smell the spikes in lynches he  doesn't have any of those visions here  we also get our first look at a sand  worm lynch's sand worms have these  mouths that part three ways well vilnius  are purely circular the teeth are also  markedly larger in the 1984 version we  never travel to seleucid secundus where  the imperial army fleet is kept we do  however see planet chitin where the  emperor lives if you've seen the  mini-series children of dune seleucid  secundus is featured there blood from  these poor souls are covered on the  sardakar the emperor's elite soldiers  who look quite different from their 1984  counterparts the betrayal of dr yui also  plays out a little different than in  1984. in vilnius he gives the atreides  sleeping pills to make their capture a  bit more easy this doesn't happen in  lynches dr yui's wife is apparently  still alive in the 2021 version and he  uses this betrayal to get her back in  1984 yui believes his wife is already  dead and this is just a ploy with this  whole poison 2 thing to get revenge the  1984 version has almost no close  quarters combat but we get lots here in  vil news with the sardikar even  utilizing these samurai-like swords it's  in this attack that duncan idaho is  killed in the 1984 version whereas  villeneuve saves his death for later on  jessica and paul's escape from the  harkonnen is pretty close to 84s but  after they land things change quite  drastically in lynch's version they are  quickly united with stilgar and the  fremen but villeneuve decides to have  them team up with kinds and take shelter  at a nearby ecological station it's here  that duncan idaho has his last stand  believe it or not we never see the baron  eat in the 1984 version but we do in  2021's poison tooth scene in 84 lato  hallucinates and breaks the tooth in  pider's face not the baron the baron  comes out pretty much uninjured here  whereas in the 2021 version it has him  recuperating for weeks in this black goo  i'm curious if this black goo is related  to that stuff that comes out of the baby  sandworms that we see later in the 1984  version perhaps it has some healing  property like duncan kynes is also given  way more screen time here she helps  usher paul and jessica to the fremen and  even dies in the process doing so she  calls forth a sand worm using a thumper  and looks as though she's preparing to  ride one before she is slaughtered by  the sarda car not seen in the 84 version  is paul's vision of him fighting  alongside the fremen against the sardar  car with these blue eyes this hints at  events in part 2 where he'll take on the  harkonnen and emperor it's easy to miss  but you can also see a sand worm in the  back in both versions paul and the  frerman control the worms in their  battle against the oppressors i should  also mention the books that kines is  cheney's father so not exactly sure how  this will play out going forward doom  2021 also does a better job at  foreshadowing events beyond dune itself  paul has a nightmare vision about a  warrior religion that waves the atreides  banner in his father's name this is  pointing to events in dune messiah and  children of dune and who knows if dune  is wildly successful there are plenty of  more books to mine material from there's  also this ecological station where kinds  talks about a process that could turn  the sands of dune into a lush green  paradise when paul becomes emperor he'll  start this process paul and the others  talk about how the attack on house of  tradies may cause an all-out war between  the emperor and various houses of the  landsrod but now that the emperor and  harkonnen control the spice such a war  would be very difficult to avoid a war  of this scale paul suggests he could  marry one of the emperor's daughters  since the emperor has no male heirs it's  a wild idea that is quickly brushed  aside but one that foreshadows paul  eventually marrying princess ireland the  emperor's daughter if you haven't seen  my children of dune video i go into that  in more depth i also love the scene  where duncan idaho bows to paul as the  new duke not seen in 84 it's a very  small scene but it carries a lot of  weight there's no such sandstorm copter  chase in 1984 a chase which lands them  in the far reaches of arrakis where  they're chased off by a sand worm i'll  go into more detail in my ending  explained about this scene but man it  really seemed like this worm was  laughing at him  what are you laughing at me for  something not seen in the 1984 version  is the bene gesture at sign language  which paul and jessica used to secretly  communicate this is however used in  children of dune between iran and the  reverend mother eventually paul and  jessica stumble upon a foreman tribe led  by stilgar there's no real fight here  between jessica and stilgar like we see  in the 2021 version she merely takes  stillgaard by the throat which prompts  james to invoke the amtol rule a fight  to the death it's also here that paul is  introduced to cheney the woman from his  dreams and she thinks he's going to get  his ass kicked in this fight paul ends  up killing james even after sparing him  three times with paul victorious the  2021 version ends with paul deciding to  stay on arrakis and fight the emperor  and hearken him if you're curious what  happens next check out my dune 1984  video which covers the events likely to  be seen in dune part 2. there you have  it some of the major differences between  the two dunes i hope you enjoyed the  video be sure to like subscribe and i  have a whole other playlist with other  cool comparison videos thanks for  watching and for more bad takes you can  always follow me on twitter and  instagram at think story yt until next  time remember daddy loves you very much

